{#
whats_new/_boot.html.twig — what opens What's new by itself after an update (#165).

An empty element carrying ui--modal and whats-new--autostart, the way
onboarding/_boot.html.twig opens setup. Rendered only when WhatsNewGlobal says
so: a release is running that this person has not been shown, they have not
asked for quiet, and setup is not on screen. Drawing the dialog records the
release as seen, so the next page load renders nothing here.

Size "split" is the max-w-5xl preset in _modal.html.twig: the release list
beside the notes.
#}
{% if whatsNew.opensByItself %}
    <div
        data-controller="ui--modal whats-new--autostart"
        data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_whats_new') }}"
        data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'whats_new.title'|trans }}"
        data-ui--modal-size-value="split"
        data-whats-new--autostart-release-value="{{ whatsNew.running }}"
        hidden
    ></div>
{% endif %}
